  "_comment": "Copy this file to config.json in this directory (gitignored). The runners use config.json when it exists, otherwise this template. This is not the repo-root config.json. suites are zh (zhbench.py, ~500 Chinese characters), en (enbench.py, ~500 English words), and doc (docbench.py, README to a tutorial). models.*.enabled defaults to true; set false to keep an id listed without running it. effort is only for claude. output_dir is relative to the repo root unless absolute. A run adds or updates only the models it actually runs. Keys already stored in outputs/reports/*.json stay even if you remove them here. publish defaults to true: run.py still writes the markdown posts, then runs the website update (publish.py via update.ps1 / update.sh). Set publish to false or pass --no-publish to skip only that live push. Cursor entries are one id per model family (the -high id, otherwise the bare id), not every fast/thinking variant, and not Claude ids (those are under claude, using the Claude CLI's own ids). Codex hidden slugs gpt-reserve and codex-auto-review are omitted. Previously run ids stay even when a CLI no longer lists them."
